      "U4 follows the GL5528 row of Senba's GL55 series manual: R = R10 * (lux / 10)^-0.6. The manual defines the 0.6 slope between 10 lx and 100 lx; this model extends the same line down to 1 lx, the lower edge of the manual's illuminance-resistance figure.",
      "R10 is 15 kΩ, the midpoint of the manual's 10-20 kΩ light-resistance range at 10 lx. The manual gives no typical value.",
      "3V3 is an ideal 3.3 V source. R6 (10 kΩ) and C7 (100 nF) use their nominal BOM values.",
